{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.999936Z","id":"5d9fb1b06dbbeb2d292deb3dd7c9b7dfac395105ce317b1c5740571e3aa1aef9","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/mod.rs:536-548, record 4c42016b.\n\nfile_url returns None when not cfg(unix) (url::Url::from_file_path does not exist on wasm32-unknown-unknown), so an export rendered by a hosted build names a project path without its file:// link, where the native daemon gives one. If hosted exports are served, build the URL portably (Url::parse(\"file:///\") and path_segments_mut, matching from_file_path's encoding of SPECIAL_PATH_SEGMENT and its handling of `..`).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":535},"end":{"line":547},"content_hash":"73804433eb012ef149abf1d37d366cf3988131fac12b6a558c31a7c7f396dfca"},"summary":"Off unix, exports render no file:// URL for an absolute path","tags":["wasm","revisit:hosted toolpath exports","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:32:34.250424Z","id":"da8ce607d1c5ff5a0963cc54b24677fa6fad737f4db36d01eb619da1fa77b9a7","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/mod.rs:536-548, record 4c42016b.\n\nfile_url returns None when not cfg(unix) (url::Url::from_file_path does not exist on wasm32-unknown-unknown), so an export rendered by a hosted build names a project path without its file:// link, where the native daemon gives one. If hosted exports are served, build the URL portably (Url::parse(\"file:///\") and path_segments_mut, matching from_file_path's encoding of SPECIAL_PATH_SEGMENT and its handling of `..`).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":551},"end":{"line":563},"content_hash":"73804433eb012ef149abf1d37d366cf3988131fac12b6a558c31a7c7f396dfca"},"summary":"Off unix, exports render no file:// URL for an absolute path","supersedes":"5d9fb1b06dbbeb2d292deb3dd7c9b7dfac395105ce317b1c5740571e3aa1aef9","tags":["wasm","revisit:hosted toolpath exports","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/redact.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:19:16.838434Z","id":"aec9b85f0f5cdf7d6c889928c525d4290a2a744cebce8b78bbea140c2cf05bf3","body":{"detail":"Commit 652f225fcffa (version restore audit fields) also added `\"db_read_grants\"` to fields_class as Class::Safe. At that commit no code writes a db_read_grants field into an artifact.update record: the field belongs to the cross-app read grant work (migration 24, crates/clax-core/src/store/grants.rs), still uncommitted when 652f225fcffa landed. Whether grant contents (artifact IDs of granted readers) are Safe under every redaction option is a decision for that work, and toolpath/tests.rs (the export test around line 1600 that asserts no unclassified fields) does not exercise it. Whoever lands the grant store should test this classification with a recorded grant change, or move the line into that commit's scope.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":313},"end":{"line":313},"content_hash":"655c2658889e9a0dcd807bc7f24dc2468211c3b80066f0d33453185f050cd26e"},"summary":"db_read_grants is classified Safe in artifact.update fields with no code that emits it and no test in the commit that added it","tags":["redaction","review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:19:16.838627Z","id":"6ee14b0ee7dd0b75ab9e86e44bc4d701eeba6d73439da23eea6c586bdd93abcc","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/redact.rs:225 classifies version.publish `restored_from` as Safe, which is right for a version number. The test that walks every recorded audit row and asserts redact::unclassified is empty (crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs, around line 1620) builds its history without Store::restore_version, and the restore tests in crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs check the stored body, not its redaction. Adding a restore to that fixture would pin the class.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1590},"end":{"line":1625},"content_hash":"f4df98f81f2f3085daeb071c708e2b3ccf96a632b353ab3a48471dcb75ea8503"},"summary":"The every-kind export test records no restore, so nothing fails if restored_from loses its redaction class","tags":["tests","review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/redact.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:25:37.013567Z","id":"94030b06f4e221c812031e71c59b32d7f369e435494c4ba9f2aa54f94fd6511a","body":{"detail":"grant_record writes artifact.update with fields.db_read_grants = {\"grant\"|\"revoke\": <source artifact ID>} and artifact2_id = source. An artifact ID is Safe under every Redaction option (no_text, no_names, no_paths), so the class is right. What is missing is a recorded grant and revoke in the fixture of the every-kind export test (crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs around 1590-1625), so a renamed field or a lost class fails a test.","kind":"comment","references":"aec9b85f0f5cdf7d6c889928c525d4290a2a744cebce8b78bbea140c2cf05bf3","summary":"The emitter now exists (crates/clax-core/src/store/grants.rs:40-50, commit 652f225fcffa); the classification is still untested by the export test","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:25:37.013584Z","id":"45e02a810539886d9cc4a3f399b33dff295671e5be0ea867efbb85d4a7d5976f","body":{"detail":"The same fixture gap leaves fields.db_read_grants (record aec9b85f) unexercised. One change covers both: call Store::restore_version and Store::grant_read / Store::revoke_read in the fixture before the audit rows are read, so redact::unclassified and assert_valid see version.publish restored_from and artifact.update fields.db_read_grants.","kind":"comment","references":"6ee14b0ee7dd0b75ab9e86e44bc4d701eeba6d73439da23eea6c586bdd93abcc","summary":"Add the restore and a grant/revoke to this fixture together","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/redact.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:28:37.695598Z","id":"32e684a2b941bad45bfb6586dab03662b5d5c7008e7f6ba52553f34c69d8aa57","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"every_recorded_kind_is_classified_and_renders_conformant (crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs) now records a grant and a revoke, which emit fields.db_read_grants. Evidence: with db_read_grants removed from fields_class the test fails with `artifact.update: unclassified [\"fields/db_read_grants\"]`; restored, it passes.","supersedes":"aec9b85f0f5cdf7d6c889928c525d4290a2a744cebce8b78bbea140c2cf05bf3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:28:37.695752Z","id":"6c57e463682f7fe5521e81552b0694599c2971a9805eeb57658f8513ce51b27a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"The every-kind export fixture now publishes a second version and restores version 1 (restored_from), and makes and revokes a read grant, asserting both are among the live events. Evidence: with restored_from removed from body_class the test fails with `version.publish: unclassified [\"restored_from\"]`; restored, it passes.","supersedes":"6ee14b0ee7dd0b75ab9e86e44bc4d701eeba6d73439da23eea6c586bdd93abcc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.453608Z","id":"0b26a9422446d0ab54ada48b8c5541cad721dd2b8592f5930c6722558d249750","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/mod.rs:536-548, record 4c42016b.\n\nfile_url returns None when not cfg(unix) (url::Url::from_file_path does not exist on wasm32-unknown-unknown), so an export rendered by a hosted build names a project path without its file:// link, where the native daemon gives one. If hosted exports are served, build the URL portably (Url::parse(\"file:///\") and path_segments_mut, matching from_file_path's encoding of SPECIAL_PATH_SEGMENT and its handling of `..`).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":552},"end":{"line":564},"content_hash":"73804433eb012ef149abf1d37d366cf3988131fac12b6a558c31a7c7f396dfca"},"summary":"Off unix, exports render no file:// URL for an absolute path","supersedes":"da8ce607d1c5ff5a0963cc54b24677fa6fad737f4db36d01eb619da1fa77b9a7","tags":["wasm","revisit:hosted toolpath exports","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
